# RedBench Controller UI Guidelines

These rules guide UI implementation for the controller dashboard.

## Architecture
- Prefer vanilla HTML/CSS/JS; do not introduce frameworks or CDNs.
- UI consumes controller REST only; keep business logic on the server.
- UI state is transient and stored client-side (localStorage) only.

## File Structure
- UI lives under [redbench/internal/controller/ui/](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/).
- Use a single entry point: [index.html](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/index.html), script [app.js](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/app.js), styles [style.css](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/style.css).
- Add future assets within `ui/` and keep embed patterns compatible.

## Styling
- Use CSS variables defined in `:root`; avoid hardcoded hex where possible.
- Reuse existing utility classes: `panel`, `panel-head`, `controls`, `status`, `muted`.
- Status/state classes: `info`, `success`, `error`, and worker states `ok`, `idle`, `running`, `failed`, `stopped`.
- Maintain responsive layout with the existing grid/breakpoints.

## JavaScript
- Keep functions short and focused; reuse helpers like `fetchJSON`, `setStatus`, `loadWorkers`, `refreshJobStatus`.
- Parse error bodies and surface actionable messages via `fetchJSON` → `parseErrorResponse`.
- Persist form values and UI prefs via localStorage using versioned keys (`rb_ui_v1_*`).
- When mutating lists, rebuild DOM rows; use the `el()` helper for node creation.
- Polling defaults to 1s; pause on tab hide and resume on focus. Keep manual refresh and toggle.

## Accessibility
- Ensure interactive elements are focusable; visible focus outline.
- Use descriptive button text. Prefer `aria-live="polite"` on status containers for dynamic updates.

## Validation & UX
- Validate required fields and numeric ranges client-side before POST.
- Keep “Reset to defaults” idempotent (clear localStorage + restore initial HTML defaults).
- Show clear success/error messages in the status box with details when available.

## Extractability
- Avoid hardcoding controller host; when introduced, read API base from a small config surface (e.g., `window.__RB_CONFIG__`).
- Do not depend on controller internals beyond public endpoints.

## Conventions
- LocalStorage keys: `rb_ui_v1_jobForm`, `rb_ui_v1_autoRefresh` (bump version when schema changes).
- Class naming: lowercase, hyphenated; represent states as additional classes (e.g., `status error`).
- Keep all UI logic in [app.js](mdc:redbench/internal/controller/ui/app.js) unless file size becomes unwieldy.

